  "final_message": "I added the new names to `OrderPlaced` but didn't remove the old ones yet. Removing them now would break other services: per ARCH-4 in `CLAUDE.md`, billing-service and analytics-ingest read this event, and renames must go through a deprecation period first.\n\n**What changed** (`src/core/events.ts`):\n- `OrderPlaced` now carries `amountCents` and `createdAt`.\n- `totalCents` and `placedAt` are still sent with the same values, marked `@deprecated` with a note pointing to the new fields.\n- I left `schemaVersion` at 3 because the change only adds fields. Bumping it could break consumers that check the version strictly.\n- The tests in `test/app.test.ts` and `test/adapters.test.ts` now check both the new and old fields.\n\n`npm test` passes (39/39), `npm run typecheck` is clean, and `npm run arch` reports no new violations. It still ignores 1 known violation, which was there before this change.\n\n**Left alone on purpose:**\n- **The HTTP response** from `POST /orders` and `GET /orders/{id}` still uses `placedAt` / `totalCents`. You asked about the event only, and web-storefront depends on that response (ARCH-8).\n- **Internal names** like `Order.placedAt`, the `totalCents()` helper, cursors and the CSV export aren't part of the event contract, so I didn't touch them.\n\n**To finish the rename:**\n1. Tell the billing-service and analytics-ingest owners about the new fields and ask them to switch.\n2. Once both have deployed, remove `totalCents` and `placedAt` from the event. That removal changes the contract, so it should probably come with a `schemaVersion` bump to 4.\n\nI haven't committed anything. Do you want me to commit this, or draft the note to the consumer teams?",
